 ### Lopes and Brodlie’s method
-A method that resolves face and internal ambiguity by using mesh vertices in the interior of the cube that lie on the trilinear interpolation isosurface [S15]. The produced mesh has an increased number of facets [S15]. Choose it when topological correctness at face and internal saddles is required and increased facet count is acceptable.
