 ## Background
-The Marching Cubes algorithm was introduced by William E. Lorensen and Harvey E. Cline in 1987 [G]. The lookup table approach was a key contribution to making the algorithm efficient by precomputing the 256 cases. The standard table has been widely adopted in graphics programming. Variants and improvements have been proposed to handle ambiguities [Improved Marching Cubes Algorithm](9090-improved-marching-cubes-algorithm.md) and optimize memory [Symmetry Mapping](869-symmetry-mapping.md).
